rs/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"At minimum we should drop Windows 7 support, but Windows 8 support officially ended almost 2 years ago so I'd say the same should apply there\r\n\r\nIf people are unable to run more modern versions of Windows I'd say they are either not going to have a good time running Godot 4.x anyway, seeing how their hardware is too old to support a 10 year old OS, or they should run something that is safer like Linux that gets security updates etc. (which would be better from a performance perspective anyway)\r\n\r\nI'd say at least that we should drop official support for pre Windows 10, as we can't expect people to test on unsafe versions, or encourage it","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106959#pullrequestreview-2889220469","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106959","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106959#pullrequestreview-2889220469"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106959"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-02T16:47:13Z","commit_id":"617e12a6b4289d157850bf1e007d3c3e779e6be5"}]